{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' SYMBOLS.md && sed -n '1,240p' ERRORS.md && sed -n '1,260p' CONFIGS.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Dynamic Symbol Surface\n\nSource: `nm -D` and `nm -D --defined-only` on\n`c_src/build/libtranslated_rust.so`, built from the unmodified C source with\nthe default CMake configuration.\n\n## Defined API Symbols\n\n| C symbol | C type | Rust type | status |\n|----------|--------|-----------|--------|\n| `allocate_block` | `T` | `T` | [ ] |\n| `betagamma` | `T` | `T` | [ ] |\n| `compute_hash` | `T` | `T` | [ ] |\n| `create_block` | `T` | `T` | [ ] |\n| `free_block` | `T` | `T` | [ ] |\n\n## C Dynamic Dependencies\n\nThese are undefined imports, not API definitions that the Rust library must\nexport: `calloc@GLIBC_2.2.5`, `free@GLIBC_2.2.5`,\n`malloc@GLIBC_2.2.5`, and `strcpy@GLIBC_2.2.5`.\n\nThe C library also has the normal weak toolchain imports\n`_ITM_deregisterTMCloneTable`, `_ITM_registerTMCloneTable`,\n`__cxa_finalize@GLIBC_2.2.5`, and `__gmon_start__`.\n\n## Completion\n\n- [ ] The defined C symbol set minus the defined Rust symbol set is empty.\n- [ ] The Rust shared library has no undefined non-system library symbols.\n# Error Surface\n\nThe rejection rows below come from every explicit error return in\n`c_src/src/lib.c`. There are no assertions, error enums, explicit scalar range\nchecks, or public enum parameters in the C source.\n\n| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result | tested |\n|---|----------|---------------------------------------------|-------------------|--------|\n| 1 | `allocate_block` | `malloc(sizeof(MemoryBlock)) == NULL` | returns `NULL` | [ ] |\n| 2 | `allocate_block` | `calloc(count, sizeof(int)) == NULL`; `SIZE_MAX` is a deterministic overflowing request on the test platform | frees the allocated `MemoryBlock` and returns `NULL` | [ ] |\n| 3 | `betagamma` | `!mem1 || !mem2`; naturally reached when `param1 % 10` is `-9..=-6`, making `(param1 % 10) + 5` negative before conversion to `size_t`, or by an injected allocation failure | frees either non-null block and returns `-1` | [ ] |\n\n## Generic FFI Boundaries\n\nThese rows record the mandatory generic boundaries even where the C code does\nnot reject them. Fatal cases are run in isolated child processes so the\nobserved C and Rust signals can be compared.\n\n| # | function | boundary | expected C behavior | tested |\n|---|----------|----------|---------------------|--------|\n| 4 | `create_block` | `name == NULL` | process terminates with `SIGSEGV` while `strcpy` reads `name` | [ ] |\n| 5 | `create_block` | 32-byte name plus terminator, one byte beyond the 31-byte payload capacity | returns a block with all 32 name bytes copied and the requested flag; C performs an out-of-bounds terminator write before assigning `flags` | [ ] |\n| 6 | `allocate_block` | `count == 0` | returns a block of size zero when the platform's `calloc(0, ...)` returns non-null | [ ] |\n| 7 | `allocate_block` | `count == SIZE_MAX` | returns `NULL` through rejection row 2 | [ ] |\n| 8 | `free_block` | `mb == NULL` | returns normally without freeing | [ ] |\n| 9 | `free_block` | `mb != NULL` and `mb->data == NULL` | frees only `mb` and returns normally | [ ] |\n| 10 | `compute_hash` | `mb1 == NULL` | process terminates with `SIGSEGV` while reading `mb1->data` | [ ] |\n| 11 | `compute_hash` | `mb2 == NULL` with non-null `mb1` | process terminates with `SIGSEGV` while reading `mb2->data` | [ ] |\n| 12 | all entry points | out-of-range enum value | not applicable: the C API has no enum parameters | [ ] |\n# Configuration Surface\n\n## Build-Time Configurations\n\n`Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` table and `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` declares no\noptions or conditional compilation. The complete valid feature combination\nset therefore contains one member:\n\n| # | Cargo invocation | CMake configuration | status |\n|---|------------------|---------------------|--------|\n| 1 | `--no-default-features` (empty feature set) | default | [ ] |\n\n## Runtime Configurations\n\nRows are derived from the branches, loops, pointer comparisons, fixed-width\narrays, and allocation-size expression in `c_src/src/lib.c`. Scalar values not\nconstrained in a row are randomized over their complete FFI representation.\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | status |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|--------|\n| 1 | `create_block` | empty NUL-terminated name; randomized `id` and all 256 `flags` values | [ ] |\n| 2 | `create_block` | name payload length `1..=30`; randomized bytes without interior NUL, `id`, and `flags` | [ ] |\n| 3 | `create_block` | maximum in-bounds name payload length 31; randomized bytes, `id`, and `flags` | [ ] |\n| 4 | `allocate_block` | empty shape: `count == 0`; randomized `init_value` | [ ] |\n| 5 | `allocate_block` | singleton shape: `count == 1`; randomized `init_value` | [ ] |\n| 6 | `allocate_block` | many shape: `count >= 2`; randomized count and initialization sequence | [ ] |\n| 7 | `free_block` | null outer pointer (`mb == NULL`) | [ ] |\n| 8 | `free_block` | non-null outer block with null `data` | [ ] |\n| 9 | `free_block`, `allocate_block` | non-null block with non-null zero-length allocation | [ ] |\n| 10 | `free_block`, `allocate_block` | non-null block with non-null populated allocation | [ ] |\n| 11 | `compute_hash` | `mb1 < mb2` and `mb1->data < mb2->data`; expected hash 110 | [ ] |\n| 12 | `compute_hash` | `mb1 < mb2` and equal data pointers (including null); expected hash 10 | [ ] |\n| 13 | `compute_hash` | `mb1 < mb2` and `mb1->data > mb2->data`; expected hash 210 | [ ] |\n| 14 | `compute_hash` | `mb1 > mb2` and `mb1->data < mb2->data`; expected hash 120 | [ ] |\n| 15 | `compute_hash` | `mb1 > mb2` and equal data pointers (including null); expected hash 20 | [ ] |\n| 16 | `compute_hash` | `mb1 > mb2` and `mb1->data > mb2->data`; expected hash 220 | [ ] |\n| 17 | `compute_hash` | identical block pointers, which necessarily have identical data pointers; expected hash 0 | [ ] |\n| 18 | `betagamma` | zero-sized internal blocks: `param1 % 10 == -5`; randomized `param2..=param4` | [ ] |\n| 19 | `betagamma` | singleton internal blocks: `param1 % 10 == -4`; randomized `param2..=param4` | [ ] |\n| 20 | `betagamma` | many-element internal blocks: `param1 % 10` in `-3..=9`; randomized valid `param1` and `param2..=param4`, including integer boundaries | [ ] |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
